  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Practitioners&apos; Network Membership Fee 2025 and 2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: Practitioners&apos; Network Membership Fee 2025 and 2026 - Pursuant to Article 210 TFEU, the Union and the Member States are to coordinate their policies on development cooperation at Union and international level and shall consult each other on their aid programmes, including in international organisations and during international conferences. They may undertake joint action. Member States shall contribute if necessary to the implementation of Union aid programmes. The Commission is allowed to take any useful initiative to promote this coordination. This work programme is fully aligned with the 2019-2024 Commission&#xbf;s policy guidelines, which identify international partnerships and development cooperation as a major factor in projecting &#xbf;a stronger Europe in the world&#xbf;. The measure supports policy coordination activities in the general area of development policy, including the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development and its SDGs; the European Consensus on Development; the implementation of the Global Gateway strategy; development effectiveness including transparency, development financing and policy coherence for development; policy coordination with external partners in the multilateral framework; enhanced coordination between development finance institutions and export credit agencies.</narrative>
  </description>
